{"page":"TET1","gene":"TET1","accession":"Q8NFU7","protein":"Methylcytosine dioxygenase TET1","length":2136,"events":["Alternative promoter usage","Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"Q8NFU7-1","name":"1","synonyms":["TET1-FL"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Dioxygenase that plays a key role in active DNA demethylation (PubMed:28531272). Binds to promoters, particularly to those with high CG content (By similarity). In hippocampal neurons, isoform 1 regulates the expression of a unique subset of genes compared to isoform 2, although some overlap exists between both isoforms, hence differentially regulates excitatory synaptic transmission (By similarity). In hippocampal neuron cell cultures, isoform 1 controls both miniature excitatory postsynaptic current amplitude and frequency (By similarity). Isoform 1 may regulate genes involved in hippocampal-dependent memory, leading to positive regulation of memory, contrary to isoform 2 that may decrease memory (By similarity)"}],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000373644.5"],"refseq":["NM_030625.3"],"refseqProteins":["NP_085128.2"],"maneSelect":true},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q8NFU7-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q8NFU7-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":46.5,"plddt":[[0,232],[50,1],[0,353],[50,2],[70,5],[90,1],[70,1],[90,2],[70,4],[90,2],[70,1],[90,5],[70,8],[90,7],[70,5],[50,1],[0,245],[50,10],[70,14],[50,2],[0,152],[50,3],[0,14],[50,1],[0,1],[50,2],[70,10],[50,6],[0,82],[50,6],[70,3],[50,1],[70,4],[50,2],[70,1],[50,4],[0,197],[50,6],[70,5],[50,2],[70,1],[50,4],[0,2],[50,1],[0,7],[50,3],[70,3],[50,7],[70,3],[90,45],[70,1],[90,25],[70,2],[90,31],[70,4],[50,5],[70,3],[90,16],[70,3],[90,24],[70,2],[90,4],[70,2],[50,3],[70,7],[90,85],[70,2],[90,2],[70,1],[90,37],[70,5],[90,4],[70,2],[90,2],[70,23],[50,2],[0,209],[50,2],[70,8],[90,68],[70,1],[90,3],[70,1],[90,1],[70,11],[50,9],[0,38],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,1],[50,5]]}},"features":[{"type":"Region","start":528,"end":674,"description":"Sufficient for binding to genomic CpG islands"},{"type":"Zinc finger","start":584,"end":625,"description":"CXXC-type"},{"type":"Binding site","start":591,"end":591,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":594,"end":594,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":597,"end":597,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":603,"end":603,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":606,"end":606,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":609,"end":609,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":619,"end":619,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":624,"end":624,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":871,"end":871,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1422,"end":1422,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1424,"end":1424,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1482,"end":1482,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1508,"end":1508,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1510,"end":1510,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1551,"end":1551,"description":"2-oxoglutarate"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1561,"end":1561,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1563,"end":1563,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1579,"end":1579,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Region","start":1580,"end":1593,"description":"Interaction with DNA"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1588,"end":1588,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":1589,"end":1589,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Site","start":1608,"end":1609,"description":"Breakpoint for translocation to form KMT2A/MLL1-TET1 oncogene"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1648,"end":1648,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1664,"end":1664,"description":"2-oxoglutarate"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1670,"end":1670,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1672,"end":1672,"description":"Fe cation"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1674,"end":1674,"description":"Fe cation"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1677,"end":1677,"description":"substrate"},{"type":"Binding site","start":1706,"end":1706,"description":"2-oxoglutarate"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2028,"end":2028,"description":"Fe cation"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2043,"end":2045,"description":"2-oxoglutarate"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2049,"end":2051,"description":"substrate"},{"type":"Binding site","start":2059,"end":2059,"description":"Zn(2+)"}],"interfaces":{},"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q8NFU7-2","name":"2","synonyms":["TET1s","TET1-ALT"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Dioxygenase that plays a key role in active DNA demethylation (PubMed:28531272). As isoform 1, binds to promoters, particularly to those with high CG content, however displays reduced global chromatin affinity compared with isoform 1, leading to decreased global DNA demethylation compared with isoform 1 (By similarity). Contrary to isoform 1, isoform 2 localizes during S phase to sites of ongoing DNA replication in heterochromatin, causing a significant de novo 5hmC formation, globally, and more so in heterochromatin, including LINE 1 interspersed DNA repeats leading to their activation (By similarity). In hippocampal neurons, isoform 2 regulates the expression of a unique subset of genes compared to isoform 1, although some overlap between both isoforms, hence differentially regulates excitatory synaptic transmission (By similarity). In hippocampal neuron cell cultures, isoform 2 controls miniature excitatory postsynaptic current frequency, but not amplitude (By similarity). Isoform 2 may regulate genes involved in hippocampal-dependent memory, leading to negative regulation of memory, contrary to isoform 1 that may improve memory (By similarity). In immature and partially differentiated gonadotrope cells, directly represses luteinizing hormone gene LHB expression and does not catalyze 5hmC at the gene promoter (By similarity)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts with UHRF1; this interaction induces the recruitment of TET1 to replicating heterochromatin (PubMed:36056023). Interacts with DCAF1 (PubMed:36056023)"},{"topic":"Miscellaneous","text":"Produced by alternative promoter usage"}],"length":1465,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":["NM_001406371.1","NM_001406372.1"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001393300.1","NP_001393301.1"],"maneSelect":false},"segments":[[1,672,1465]],"edits":[{"start":1,"end":671,"original":"MSRSRHARPSRLVRKEDVNKKKKNSQLRKTTKGANKNVAS","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":671,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":41,"foldedMissing":41,"features":[[0,144,0],[1,42,0],[2,1,0],[3,1,0],[4,1,0],[5,1,0],[6,1,0],[7,1,0],[8,1,0],[9,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q8NFU7-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q8NFU7-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":54.9,"plddt":[[0,204],[50,3],[70,1],[50,3],[70,17],[50,3],[0,15],[50,17],[0,1],[50,1],[0,134],[70,17],[50,3],[0,81],[50,5],[70,10],[50,1],[70,2],[50,2],[70,1],[50,3],[0,194],[50,3],[70,10],[50,1],[70,1],[50,5],[0,1],[50,1],[0,7],[50,3],[70,3],[50,7],[70,3],[90,71],[70,2],[90,31],[70,4],[50,1],[70,1],[50,2],[70,4],[90,15],[70,4],[90,24],[70,2],[90,4],[70,2],[50,3],[70,7],[90,85],[70,1],[90,42],[70,4],[90,4],[70,2],[90,2],[70,24],[50,1],[0,1],[50,1],[0,207],[50,2],[70,3],[90,2],[70,3],[90,72],[70,1],[90,2],[70,11],[50,2],[70,1],[50,5],[0,32],[50,1],[0,1],[50,13]],"losingConfidence":0}},{"accession":"Q8NFU7-3","name":"3","synonyms":[],"notes":[{"topic":"Miscellaneous","text":"Produced by alternative splicing"}],"length":1305,"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":["NM_001406374.1"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001393303.1"],"maneSelect":false},"segments":[[1,1,656],[657,1488,649]],"edits":[{"start":657,"end":1487,"original":"ADFDNKPVNGPKSESMDYSRCGHGEEQKLELNPHTVENVT","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":831,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsen